			"color":"#232",
			"widgets_values":[
				"subject_definitions:\n<Subject 1> is the young woman in <Picture 1>, with dark brown hair loosely pinned up in a messy bun with wispy strands framing her face, fair skin with visible tear tracks and rosy blush on her nose and cheeks, glossy red lips, wearing long dangling pearl earrings and a champagne-colored satin cheongsam (qipao) with intricate pink rose embroidery and a pearl button at the collar.\n<Subject 2> is the street scene in <Picture 2> during golden hour: a coastal promenade in Hong Kong featuring a black-and-white street sign reading \"New Praya, Kennedy Town\" and \"堅彌地城新海旁\" with numbers \"38\" and \"28-7\", a curved red fire hydrant on the left, a yellow metal barrier, a brick-paved sidewalk in a herringbone pattern, a calm sea reflecting the sunset, distant silhouetted mountains and city skyline, and a gradient sky transitioning from soft orange at the horizon to pale blue above.\n\nsummary:\n[reference generation] The target video is a 15-second five-shot cinematic emotional short featuring <Subject 1> in a cheongsam taking photos at the sunset location of <Subject 2>. It captures a melancholic yet beautiful \"check-in\" moment, starting with her back to the camera, turning around with tear-stained makeup, adjusting her pearl earring, wiping a tear, and ending with a wide shot of her silhouette against the twilight sea. The style is Wong Kar-wai inspired filmic texture with warm golden lighting, soft focus, and no dialogue.\n\nretention_analysis:\n<Subject 1> (appears in [Shot 2], [Shot 3], [Shot 4], [Shot 5]): fully_preserved - her messy bun, tearful makeup with rosy blush, pearl earrings, and champagne rose-embroidered cheongsam are retained exactly as in <Picture 1>.\n<Subject 2> (appears in [Shot 1], [Shot 2], [Shot 3], [Shot 5]): fully_preserved - the \"New Praya, Kennedy Town\" sign, red hydrant, brick pavement, sea, and sunset sky maintain their layout and lighting atmosphere.\n\ndetailed_description:\nThe target video uses a cinematic film style reminiscent of 90s Hong Kong cinema, with heavy film grain, warm golden-hour halation, shallow depth of field, and a nostalgic orange-teal color palette. Global rules: no dialogue; <Subject 1> never holds a phone or camera visibly (implied off-screen photographer); the street sign text must remain legible; the red hydrant position is locked; distant ships are tiny and still; a gentle evening breeze moves her hair and cheongsam fabric.\n\n[Shot 1] The video opens with a static wide shot of <Subject 2> at sunset. The sky is a soft gradient of orange and blue. <Subject 1> stands in the center foreground with her back to the camera, facing the sea and the \"New Praya, Kennedy Town\" sign. She is still, her silhouette framed by the signpost and the red hydrant on the left. The wind gently ruffles the loose strands of her hair. End state: <Subject 1> standing still, back to camera, sunset glow outlining her figure.\n\n[Shot 2] At 00:03.000, the shot cuts to a medium shot from the front. <Subject 1> has turned around to face the lens. The golden sunlight hits her face from the side, highlighting the tear tracks on her cheeks and the gloss on her lips. She looks slightly startled, as if caught in a vulnerable moment, her eyes wide and watery. She slowly raises one hand to tuck a wind-blown strand of hair behind her ear, her fingers brushing against the dangling pearl earring. End state: <Subject 1> facing camera, hand near her ear, tearful expression, golden light on her face.\n\n[Shot 3] At 00:06.000, the shot cuts to a closer medium shot focusing on her upper body and the cheongsam details. She lowers her hand from her ear and brings it to her chest, delicately adjusting the pearl button at the collar of her champagne cheongsam. She looks down shyly, biting her lower lip slightly, then takes a deep breath, her chest rising visibly. She lifts her gaze back to the lens, her eyes shimmering with unshed tears. End state: <Subject 1> looking at the lens, hand resting on her collar, emotional gaze.\n\n[Shot 4] At 00:09.000, the shot cuts to an extreme close-up of <Subject 1>'s face. The background is a soft bokeh of the sunset sky. A single tear rolls down her left cheek. She slowly lifts her index finger to gently wipe the tear away, careful not to smudge her blush. Her eyes flutter closed for a brief second, then open slowly, revealing a faint, melancholic smile that doesn't quite reach her eyes. The light catches the moisture in her eyes. End state: Extreme close-up, tear wiped, faint sad smile, eyes glistening.\n\n[Shot 5] At 00:12.000, the shot cuts back to a wide shot similar to [Shot 1], but slightly lower angle. <Subject 1> is now leaning lightly against the pole of the street sign, one leg crossed over the other, posing naturally. She tilts her head back to look at the darkening sky, her profile illuminated by the last rays of sun. The scene feels quiet and resolved. She holds the pose, becoming part of the landscape. End state: Wide shot, <Subject 1> leaning on sign post, looking up at the sky, silhouette against the twilight.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nEvening seaside ambience: gentle waves lapping against the shore, a soft warm wind blowing through the microphone, distant muffled ferry horns, the subtle sound of fabric rustling in [Shot 3], and a faint, sharp inhale of breath in [Shot 4]. No distinct voices or traffic noise.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nA slow, melancholic cinematic score: a solo cello playing a long, sustained note that swells gently in [Shot 2], accompanied by sparse, echoing piano keys in [Shot 3] and [Shot 4]. The music fades out slowly in [Shot 5], leaving only the sound of the wind and waves, creating a lingering sense of nostalgia."
